course: dictionary
lesson: 9542
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Stone is a good example. In «a stone wall», stone is the hard material that rocks are made of. In a cherry with a stone, it is the hard seed in the middle.
explain: Look at the words around the word. What is it near, what is it used for, what does it look like? Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits. In «a capuchin cracks a nut with a stone like a hammer», the stone is a small piece of rock, because it is used like a hammer.
explain: A dictionary lists the meanings, but you still have to choose the right one. Stone can also be a jewel, as in «a ring with a red stone», or a unit of weight used in Britain and Ireland, where a stone is 14 pounds.
fact: Stone is a noun, and it has several meanings.
fact: A stone is a small piece of rock.
fact: Stone is the hard material rocks are made of, as in «a stone wall».
fact: A stone is the hard seed in the middle of some fruits, like a cherry or a peach.
fact: A stone is also a unit of weight used in Britain and Ireland: a stone is 14 pounds.
exercise: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone.» What is a stone here? | A unit of weight | A jewel in a ring | *A small piece of rock | A hard seed inside a fruit
exercise: «Vikings wrote with runes, letters cut into wood and stone.» What is stone in this sentence? | *The hard material rocks are made of | A small piece of rock to throw | A jewel | A hard seed inside a fruit
exercise: Ella eats a peach and finds a big hard stone in the middle. What is the stone? | A jewel | A unit of weight | A kidney stone | *The hard seed in the middle of the fruit
test: «A ring with a red stone» uses stone to mean what? | A small piece of rock | A hard seed in a fruit | A unit of weight | *A jewel
test: Dad says he weighs 10 stone. What does stone mean here? | The hard material of a wall | A jewel | *A unit of weight, 14 pounds each | A small piece of rock
exam: In the Stone Age, people made their tools from stone. What is stone in this sentence? | A jewel | A hard seed inside a fruit | A unit of weight | *The hard material rocks are made of
